From 43417a936e7728fb39bddc6bb14fa54f54f14912 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:43:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ResBackend: the resources seam (aosp-views step 0, resources
 half)

Every call from outside the resources side (android.content.res and its
helpers ResourceIndex, ArscReader, BinaryXmlParser, DomXmlResourceParser,
axml) into a member AOSP 14's android.content.res lacks, or into
ResourceIndex, now goes through com.macapk.loader.res.ResBackend; ArscRes,
its one implementation, calls the member each method stands for. The
reflective calls into ResourceIndex (resolveAttrInTheme, macapkTypeNameOf,
getStyleByName and StyleDef's fields...) go through it too. 224 sites in 27
files; no behaviour change: the UI probe, the Gallery and Sudoku screens
sweeps and FrameworkStubsTest give identical output before and after.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0185vQkPNo1ENZ3Mi9zALKd2
